<title>USA: BP says shut-in Gulf of Mexico fields back up.</title>
<headline>BP says shut-in Gulf of Mexico fields back up.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>BP Oil said Monday that all the offshore oil and gas production shut in by Hurricane Danny was back up over the weekend.</p>
<p>BP shut in most of its oil and gas production -- three of four offshore fields representing about 45,000 barrels per day of crude and 50 million cubic feet a day of natural gas -- as the storm ripped through the Gulf on Friday.</p>
<p>Evacuated staff returned on Saturday and turned back on all production, expected for &quot;one of two things shut in from before the storm,&quot; said Hugh Depland, a BP spokesman.</p>
<p>((--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620))</p>
